#: rc.cpp:1
msgid ""
"<h1>Keyboard Layout</h1> Here you can choose your keyboard layout and model. "
"The 'model' refers to the type of keyboard that is connected to your "
"computer, while the keyboard layout defines \"which key does what\" and may "
"be different for different countries.<p>In addition to the 'Primary Layout', "
"which will be used as the default, you can specify additional layouts, which "
"you can easily switch between using the KDE panel.\n"
msgstr ""

#: rc.cpp:2 rc.cpp:13 rc.cpp:23
msgid "Layout"
msgstr ""

#: rc.cpp:3
msgid "&Enable keyboard layouts"
msgstr ""

#: rc.cpp:4 rc.cpp:40 rc.cpp:62
msgid "Alt+E"
msgstr ""

#: rc.cpp:6
msgid "Available layouts:"
msgstr ""

#: rc.cpp:7
msgid "Active layouts:"
msgstr ""

#: rc.cpp:8
msgid "Keyboard &model:"
msgstr ""

#: rc.cpp:9
msgid ""
"Here you can choose a keyboard model. This setting is independent of your "
"keyboard layout and refers to the \"hardware\" model, i.e. the way your "
"keyboard is manufactured. Modern keyboards that come with your computer "
"usually have two extra keys and are referred to as \"104-key\" models, which "
"is probably what you want if you don't know what kind of keyboard you have.\n"
msgstr ""

#: rc.cpp:10
msgid "Include latin layout"
msgstr ""

#: rc.cpp:11
msgid ""
"If after you switch to this layout some keyboard shortcuts based on latin "
"keys do not work try to enable this option."
msgstr ""

#: rc.cpp:14 rc.cpp:24
msgid "Keymap"
msgstr ""

#: rc.cpp:15
msgid ""
"You can select an arbitrary number of keyboard layouts. If more than one "
"layouts have been selected, the KDE panel will offer a docked flag. By "
"clicking on this flag you can easily switch between layouts."
msgstr ""

#: rc.cpp:16
msgid "Layout variant:"
msgstr ""

#: rc.cpp:17
msgid ""
"Here you can choose a variant of your primary keyboard layout. Layout "
"variants usually represent different key maps for the same language. For "
"example, Ukrainian layout might have four variants: basic, winkeys (as in "
"Windows), typewriter (as in typewriters) and phonetic (each Ukrainian letter "
"is placed on a transliterated latin one).\n"
msgstr ""

#: rc.cpp:18
msgid "Add >>"
msgstr ""

#: rc.cpp:19
msgid "<< Remove"
msgstr ""

#: rc.cpp:25
msgid ""
"This is the list of available keyboard layouts for your X Window system. To "
"be able to choose layout you want with keyboard indicator select it and "
"press \"Add\" button."
msgstr ""

